## Original Content
<p>　　新华社纽约6月3日电（记者徐静）行业数据公司美国沃兹情报公司3日发布的数据显示，美国5月轻型汽车销量出现五年来最大跌幅。</p> <p>　　数据显示，美国5月轻型汽车销量为1565万辆，比4月修正后的1725万辆下降约160万辆，为2020年4月以来最大降幅。美国3月轻型汽车销量为1783万辆。</p> <p>　　美国政府对进口汽车加征25%关税的措施4月3日生效。分析人士认为，美国消费者3月、4月赶在价格上涨前购买车辆，是导致5月销售惨淡的原因之一。</p>

## Summary
US auto sales in May plummeted, dropping by approximately 1.6 million units from April to 15.65 million, marking the largest decline in five years. This downturn is linked to consumers accelerating purchases in March and April ahead of new 25% tariffs on imported vehicles that took effect on April 3. The tariffs contributed to a slump in sales in May, reflecting market adjustments.

## Key Points
- US light vehicle sales in May fell to 15.65 million, a decline of about 1.6 million from April's 17.25 million.
- The drop is the largest monthly decrease since April 2020, indicating a significant market downturn.
- Consumers purchased more vehicles in March and April to avoid higher prices from impending tariffs.
- 25% tariffs on imported cars were implemented on April 3, directly impacting sales trends.
- Sales in March were higher at 17.83 million, showing pre-tariff buying behavior.


